# Open Engineering Playbook CODEOWNERS template for GitHub. Copy to .github/CODEOWNERS.
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Rules:
# - Use teams (@org/team), never individuals who might leave.
# - The last matching pattern wins, so put the general rule first.
# - Every owning team should have at least 3 members.
# - The team ruleset (docs/repository-rules/default-branch.json after
#   tools/adopt.sh) turns on "require review from code owners". The solo
#   ruleset does not, because nobody else can review.
# Replace @your-org/... with your own teams.

# Default owner for everything
*                               @your-org/service-team

# Database migrations: service team plus data specialists
/migrations/                    @your-org/service-team @your-org/data-platform
/db/                            @your-org/service-team @your-org/data-platform

# Security-sensitive code
/src/auth/                      @your-org/service-team @your-org/security-champions
/src/crypto/                    @your-org/security-champions

# Infrastructure as code
/infra/                         @your-org/platform
*.tf                            @your-org/platform

# CI, release automation and repository rules
/.github/workflows/             @your-org/platform @your-org/security-champions
/.github/dependabot.yml         @your-org/platform
/release-please-config.json     @your-org/platform
/.release-please-manifest.json  @your-org/platform
/docs/repository-rules/         @your-org/platform @your-org/security-champions

# Agent instructions: a change here changes how code gets written
/AGENTS.md                      @your-org/platform @your-org/security-champions
**/AGENTS.md                    @your-org/platform

# Ownership of ownership: changes here need platform review
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @your-org/platform

# Public documentation
/docs/                          @your-org/service-team @your-org/tech-writers
